"The Lost City."

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.968
Give it up for Daniel Radcliffe,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.200
-Hello!

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.234
-♪ Ice ♪
-Now, Tariq --

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.167
-Thanks.
-Tariq, tell them how it works.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:35.234
♪♪

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.367
-[Laughing] Well!

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:39.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.467
♪♪

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:45.033
-I'll alternate asking each
of you the trivia questions.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.667
-Uh-huh.
-If you answer wrong,

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:51.033
I'll pour a pitcher of ice water
down the tube of death,

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:54.167
delivering it directly
to your crotch.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.601
-Oh, well. Okay.

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:58.267
-However,
if you answer correctly,

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.868
your opponent gets iced instead.

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:01.868
Are you ready?

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.434
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:04.968
-Yes!
-Let's do this.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.501
-Daniel, the first question
is for you.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:13.934
Your new movie, "The Lost City,"
is about a romance novelist --

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.534
-You can't ask him
about his own movie!

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:18.534
-Which of the following
is not the name

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:22.033
of a real romance novel
that you can buy right now

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.901
if you were to go book shopping
for a romance novel

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.834
at the romance novel shop?

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:31.701
Is it "A," "The Bull Rider's
Christmas Baby?"

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.067
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:36.868
"B," "My Zombie Werewolf
Mistress?"

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:37.868
-Oh...

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:41.767
Or "C,"
"But...You're a Horse"?

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.767
-Aw, I really thought
these would be gettable.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:48.601
-Yes.
-Um -- okay, I mean,

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:53.267
I'm gonna go "C,"
"But...You're a Horse."

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:55.367
-The correct answer was...
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:57.767
"My Zombie Werewolf Mistress."

00:01:57.767 --> 00:01:59.033
[ Audience ohs ]

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.000
-Give it to me!
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.133
-Daniel, that is incorrect.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:06.901
It's time for you to get iced.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:08.334
-Do it.

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:11.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:14.067
♪♪

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.100
Okay. Okay.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.200
This is -- yeah.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.334
Yeah.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:20.567
-It's real?

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.367
-Oh, it's okay. It keeps going.
There's a lot.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.133
It's still coming.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.467
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:26.601
-Good. Good.
-Wow.

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:27.601
-Wow.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:28.901
Okay.
-Yeah! That's right!

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.501
-Great.
-We're out of time.

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:31.601
We'll be right back.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.334
-Okay, time for
the next question.

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:38.167
Jimmy, this one is for you.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:41.267
"The Lost City" also stars

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.300
the always-effervescent
Sandra Bullock.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.767
-Mm.
In Sandra's classic movie

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:51.267
"Speed," the bus will explode
if it falls below what speed?

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.534
-I know this.
-Now, I think the speed limit,

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:56.968
I would say is probably --
50 would be normal.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:59.000
55, Sammy Hagar.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.601
60 is too fast.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:03.534
But 60 is --
is actually speeding.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:04.667
♪♪

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.467
-Jimmy, what is your answer?!
-Wait --

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:10.000
If 50 is going normal,
55 is normal maybe.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.234
60 is speeding.
My answer is 60.

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:13.601
'Cause it's called "Speed."

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:14.767
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:17.334
-The correct answer
was 50 miles per hour.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:18.934
-Oh, God!
-Yes!

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.834
-Jimmy, you get the ice.
-Okay, thank you.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:26.834
["Ice, Ice Baby" plays ]

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:32.534
♪♪

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:38.200
♪♪

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.901
-Oh, my gosh.
-♪ Ice ♪

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:41.901
-Daniel, back to you.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:44.767
The story
of the lost city of Atlantis

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:47.534
originally comes from
the ancient Greeks.

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:50.934
Atlantis is, of course, a
fictional island mentioned in --

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.400
-Yeah, yeah, yeah!
What's the question?!

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.934
-An allegory on the hubris of
nations in the work of Plato.

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.400
Which of these things finds --
-Ask the question, please!

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.767
-Which of these things you'd --
-Ask the question!

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.667
-Which of these things you'd
find in your kitchen is --

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:05.701
gets its name
from an ancient Roman God?

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:06.701
-Okay.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.167
-Is it "A," refrigerator...

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:12.100
-"B," faucet, or "C," cereal.
-"B", a faucet...

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.501
or "C," cereal.

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:17.400
-Um -- [ Stammers ]

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.667
Refrigerator!

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.701
[ Buzzer ]
-The correct answer was cereal.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:22.901
♪♪

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:24.300
-Okay.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.033
-Named after Ceres,
the Goddess of grain.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.267
Daniel, you got it wrong
yet again.

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:32.701
Time for you to get iced!

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:35.601
♪♪

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.501
-Come on, spread it 'round.
Oh, yeah.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.367
[ Laughter ]
There you go.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:40.634
-The second one --
-Yeah.

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.000
-The second one is harder
than the first one, right?

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.634
-It really is -- it really is --
it's very right leg heavy,

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:45.534
but it's an incredibly cold
right leg.

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:48.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.467
-♪ Ice ♪

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:51.601
-Way back in 1997 --

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:52.834
-Oh, my heavens.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.868
-The world was first introduced
to a young wizard

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.567
with a heart of gold.

00:04:57.567 --> 00:05:02.100
His name, Harry Potter.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.267
-Yes!

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:04.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:07.634
-In "Harry Potter
and the Prisoner of Azkaban" --

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:10.100
-Yes, of course.
-What spell do you cast

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.467
